#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:2
msgid "Documenting tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:4
msgid ""
"You can add help text to your tasks by adding the ``help`` option to the "
"task definition, like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:6
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.test]\n"
"help = \"Run the test suite\"\n"
"cmd  = \"pytest --cov=poethepoet\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.serve]\n"
"help   = \"Run the app in debug mode\"\n"
"script = \"my_app.service:run(debug=True)\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.tunnel]\n"
"help  = \"Create an SSH tunnel to the production server\"\n"
"shell = \"ssh -N -L 0.0.0.0:8080:$prod_host:8080 $prod_host &\"\n"
"args   = [\n"
"  {name = \"prod_host\", help = \"Hostname of the production server\", "
"default = \"myapp.com\"}\n"
"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:23
msgid ""
"This help text will be displayed alongside the task name in the list of "
"configured tasks when ``poe`` is run without specifying a task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:25
msgid ""
"<div class=\"highlight-sh notranslate\">\n"
"<div class=\"highlight\">\n"
"<pre>$ poe --help\n"
"<strong>Poe the Poet</strong> (version <span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">0.43.0</"
"span>)\n"
"\n"
"<strong>Usage:</strong>\n"
"  <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">poe</span> [global options] task "
"[task arguments]\n"
"\n"
"<strong>Global options:</strong>\n"
"  <strong>-h, --help [TASK]</strong>     Show this help page and exit, "
"optionally supply a\n"
"                        task.\n"
"  <strong>--version</strong>             Print the version and exit\n"
"  <strong>-v, --verbose</strong>         Increase output (repeatable)\n"
"  <strong>-q, --quiet</strong>           Decrease output (repeatable)\n"
"  <strong>-d, --dry-run</strong>         Print the task contents but don't "
"actually run it\n"
"  <strong>-C, --directory PATH</strong>  Specify where to find the pyproject."
"toml\n"
"  <strong>-e, --executor EXECUTOR</strong>\n"
"                        Override the default task executor\n"
"  <strong>-X, --executor-opt KEY[=VALUE]</strong>\n"
"                        Set executor configuration for this run.\n"
"  <strong>--ansi</strong>                Force enable ANSI output\n"
"  <strong>--no-ansi</strong>             Force disable ANSI output\n"
"\n"
"<strong>Configured tasks:</strong>\n"
"  <span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">test</span>           Run the test suite\n"
"  <span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">serve</span>          Run the app in debug "
"mode\n"
"  <span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">tunnel</span>         Create an SSH tunnel "
"to the production server\n"
"   <span style=\"color:#4B78CC\">--prod_host</span>  Hostname of the "
"production server [default: myapp.com]\n"
"</pre>\n"
"</div>\n"
"</div>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:60
msgid "Display help for a single task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:62
msgid ""
"Passing the ``--help`` option normally has the same effect as running poe "
"with no arguments. However you can also supply the name of a task to display "
"documentation for just that task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:64
msgid ""
"<div class=\"highlight-sh notranslate\">\n"
"<div class=\"highlight\">\n"
"<pre>$ poe --help tunnel\n"
"\n"
"<strong>Description:</strong>\n"
"  Create an SSH tunnel to the production server\n"
"\n"
"<strong>Usage:</strong>\n"
"  <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">poe</span> [global options] "
"<span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">tunnel</span> [named arguments] -- [free "
"arguments]\n"
"\n"
"<strong>Named arguments:</strong>\n"
"  <span style=\"color:#4B78CC\">--prod_host</span>    Hostname of the "
"production server [default: myapp.com]\n"
"</pre>\n"
"</div>\n"
"</div>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:83
msgid "Grouping tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:85
msgid ""
"You can organize tasks into groups by defining them within group tables. "
"This makes it easier to navigate large task lists and allows you to apply "
"shared configuration (like an executor) to all tasks in a group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:87
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.test]\n"
"help = \"Run the tests\"\n"
"cmd = \"pytest\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.groups.server]\n"
"heading = \"Application Serving\"\n"
"executor = { type = \"uv\", group = \"server\" }  # Tasks in this group will "
"run with uv's \"server\" dependency-group\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.groups.server.tasks.dev]\n"
"help = \"Run the app in debug mode\"\n"
"cmd  = \"uvicorn my_app:app --reload\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.groups.server.tasks.prod]\n"
"help = \"Run the app in production mode\"\n"
"cmd  = \"uvicorn my_app:app\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.groups.testing]\n"
"heading = \"Testing & Quality\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.groups.testing.tasks.test]\n"
"help = \"Run the test suite\"\n"
"cmd  = \"pytest --cov=my_app\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.groups.testing.tasks.lint]\n"
"help = \"Run the linter\"\n"
"cmd  = \"ruff check .\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:116
msgid ""
"When you run ``poe`` without specifying a task, ungrouped tasks appear "
"first, followed by groups sorted alphabetically by group name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:118
msgid ""
"<div class=\"highlight-sh notranslate\">\n"
"<div class=\"highlight\">\n"
"<pre><strong>Configured tasks:</strong>\n"
"  <span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">test</span>           Run the tests\n"
"\n"
"<span style=\"color:#98C379\">Application Serving</span>\n"
"  <span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">dev</span>            Run the app in debug "
"mode\n"
"  <span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">prod</span>           Run the app in "
"production mode\n"
"\n"
"<span style=\"color:#98C379\">Testing &amp; Quality</span>\n"
"  <span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">unit</span>           Run the test suite\n"
"  <span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">lint</span>           Run the linter\n"
"</pre>\n"
"</div>\n"
"</div>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:137
msgid ""
"Group names must consist of only alphanumeric characters, dashes, or "
"underscores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:141
msgid "Group options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:143
msgid ""
"**heading**: A human-readable name for the group displayed in help output. "
"If not specified, the group name is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:144
msgid ""
"**executor**: Executor configuration that applies to all tasks in the group. "
"Group executor config has higher precedence than project level, and lower "
"precedence than task level config."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:145
msgid "**tasks**: A table of task definitions within the group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:149
msgid "Merging groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/help_guide.rst:151
msgid ""
"When an :ref:`included config file<Running tasks from another file>` defines "
"a group with the same name as one in the main project config, the tasks from "
"both are merged under a single heading. Only group config (e.g. heading and "
"executor) from the config file with the highest precedence is preserved when "
"merging groups."
msgstr ""
